MAYOR OF BLITAR,

Considering: a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture, discrimination or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that women and children are vulnerable groups who tend to experience Violence, therefore they need to receive legal Protection;
c. that based on the provisions in Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015, women's empowerment and child protection are governmental affairs that must be implemented by Regional Governments;
d. that the implementation of Protection for Women and Child Victims of Violence in Blitar City has not been optimal, therefore institutional strengthening is needed and there needs to be regulation that can guarantee its implementation in accordance with applicable provisions;
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c and letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence;

In View of: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 17 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Small City Regions within the Province of East Java, Central Java and West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 42) as amended by Law Number 13 of 1954 concerning Amendment to Law Number 16 and Number 17 of 1950 (Former Republic of Indonesia) Concerning the Establishment of Large Cities and Small Cities in Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1954 Number 40, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 551);
3. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 3143);
4. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 3668);
5. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 3886);
6. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143); as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
7. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
8. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
9. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
10. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);
11. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
12. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
13. Government Regulation Number 48 of 1982 concerning Amendment to the Territorial Boundaries of the Level II Municipality of Blitar (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1982 Number 75, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3243);
14. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia number 64);
15. Presidential Regulation Number 87 of 2014 concerning Implementation Regulations of Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 199);
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Implementation of Women's Protection;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Implementation of Child Protection;
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 56);
18. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
19. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;
